WEBVTT

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.950
Is that how you act when 
you receive an order, punk?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.180
This is for our motherland.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.040
If you die, be content. 
Don't let death stop you!

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:18.840
Sir...

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.390
Sir, if I may, it seems foolish to be content

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.180
with dying in what amounts 
to a training exercise!

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.090
Besides...

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.850
I don't think these men 
are fit to be scouts.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.200
What "amounts to" a training exercise?

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.320
Tobisaki!

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.790
Are you, a soldier who swore 
allegiance to the army,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:43.280
saying that your superior 
officer's orders are "foolish"?!

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.770
No, sir, I'm not! I just—

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.650
You "just" nothing!

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.610
Stop complaining and move out!

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.200
Grab him!

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.370
Violence against a superior 
officer! Refusing orders!

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.510
Are you the one they called "untrainable?"

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.420
Any plans for after you quit the army?

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.150
Good question.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.530
Maybe I'll move to Manchuria

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.580
and become a roving bandit.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:51.960
If you feel up to it, come take my exam.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.830
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.100
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.350
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:04.350
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.430
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.430
<i>established a clandestine 
spy training agency.</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.770
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.830
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.240
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.940
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.870
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.790
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.250
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:34.630
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.950
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.780
Somebody call the police!

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:21.110
Episode 12 - XX (Double Cross)

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.440
Call the police!

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.910
What's going on?

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.730
He's dead?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.580
"I've lost all hope. I want to die."

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.880
Was he killed?

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.740
<i>The target I was watching died.</i>

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.940
<i>It was an inexcusable failure.</i>

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.970
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.970
<b>1939, Spring</b>

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.730
The deceased is a German 
man named Karl Schneider.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.950
Publicly, he was a writer 
for <i>Berlin Allgemeine</i>,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.650
but was a suspected double agent
for Germany and the Soviet Union.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:04.150
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:01.450
On the day of the incident, Schneider 
bought flowers from a street vendor

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.580
and headed for the apartment of his lover, 
Nogami Yuriko, a theater performer.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:07.910
They met about a year ago

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.700
through a friend of Nogami's and began dating.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.370
Schneider furnished the 
apartment in question for Yuriko.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.550
Nogami was out that day,

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:22.600
but just after 3 PM, 
she returned with her friend

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.140
and fellow performer, Yasuhara Miyoko.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:26.830
According to the report,

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.680
they'd arranged to go eat cake together.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.720
As far as Schneider's death goes, 
the police ruled it a suicide

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:37.130
and will not be investigating further.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.390
How likely is it that Schneider 
realized you were watching him,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.130
decided he had no chance of 
escape, and killed himself?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.800
Schneider was a top-class spy.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.910
The thought of him choosing death

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.620
seems rather unnatural to me.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.080
However, the suicide note's a problem.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.420
How do you explain it?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.300
The handwriting analysis 
said he wrote it himself.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.090
In short, Odagiri,

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.380
you believe someone killed Schneider,

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.970
and the note was forged?

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.630
Given that he was a double agent,

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:19.180
it wouldn't have been odd for either 
Germany or the Soviets to go after him.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.690
All I'm saying is that we need 
to consider the possibility.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.170
But your contributions have already given us

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.610
enough information to reject the idea.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.480
You heard screaming a moment after

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.600
the woman and her friend came home.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.120
No one exited through that door before then.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.580
What was the target's cause of death?

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.970
Asphyxiation from cyanide poisoning.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.840
The same compound was found on the 
glass of wine he'd been drinking from.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:53.690
You're saying that when Schneider died,

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.020
you didn't notice anything at all?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.570
This Schneider...

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:13.780
He was fluent in English, wasn't he?

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.710
Is that from him testing the pen?

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.240
Maybe.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:22.890
But it also looks like two crosses side by side.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.570
In English, "double-cross" means "to betray."

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.210
Someone betrayed Schneider...

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:32.140
Or <i>he</i> betrayed <i>them</i>.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.630
What do you think?

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.180
Whatever the case, we have to 
take control of his spy network.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.150
Kaminaga, investigate everyone who 
went to Schneider's house again.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.360
Hatano, double-check the actual suicide note.

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:50.160
Miyoshi, check the latest developments 
at the German and Soviet embassies.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.200
Amari, investigate any native

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.620
English speakers who lived near Schneider.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.700
Tazaki, look into the wine import channels...

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.550
Fukumoto...

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.040
What do you want me to do?

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.470
Investigate the woman who was at the scene.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.500
The woman?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.720
But she...

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.910
<i>Nogami Yuriko had an airtight alibi.</i>

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.140
<b>Shinjuku Akakaze Circle</b>

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.320
<i>At the time I suspect Schneider died,</i>

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.070
<i>she was in a dress rehearsal 
with her theater company.</i>

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.840
<i>According to witness testimonies,</i>

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:36.080
<i>she was never off the stage 
for more than five minutes.</i>

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.720
I leave tomorrow.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.940
We may never meet again.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.000
Knowing that, will you still wait for me?

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.100
I will.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.570
I'll forever be here, waiting for your return.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.930
So please, come back...

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:03.630
I loved him with all my heart.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:07.470
So much that I want them to 
live the life they truly want.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.190
I will disappear quietly.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.110
Even if a future

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.570
of darkness and solitude awaits.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.260
It will

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.530
still be proof that I lived!

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.590
Great show!

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.320
Today's performance was amazing!

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:39.300
Miyoko-san, you've really got a flair for this.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.280
Thank you.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:44.600
Yuriko-san was the real star, though.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.730
In spite of what happened...

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.410
She was just splendid.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:54.490
<b>Tokyo 
Flower 
Girl</b>

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.160
I wonder if Yuriko-san's all right....

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.980
Excuse me, sir?

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:31.540
Is anything the matter?

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:33.090
Oh, no.

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.180
Yasuhara-san's quite popular, isn't she?

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:38.370
Look at all these flowers for her.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.950
Oh, yes, thank you.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:48.910
<b>Congratulations to
Yasuhara Miyoko</b>

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.840
It's just talent, I suppose.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:46.350
Miyoko-san's gotten better and better...

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.590
These days, she's our marquee actress.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.560
Are those flowers for Yasuhara-san, too?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.420
What a calming scent.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.720
Yes,

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:00.840
they're Miyoko-san's favorite flower.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.300
To be honest, after some time,

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:07.780
a nearby florist takes Miyoko-san's 
flowers off our hands.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.370
I hope you're not offended.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.350
They're beautiful and shouldn't go to waste.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.780
<b>Shinjuku Akakaze Circle</b>

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:16.050
I understand.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:21.740
<b>Café Suzunari</b>

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:30.280
No invisible ink. The paper 
was bought from a local store.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.970
No suspicious activity from

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.400
the people who went into Schneider's home.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:45.200
I looked at the wine importing companies.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.680
None were connected to an intelligence agency.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.970
Nothing unusual at the German 
and Soviet embassies,

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.360
but someone new may have taken 
over Schneider's spy network.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.980
Why are you reporting to me?!

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:00.580
Why...

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.620
This is your case.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.590
My... case?

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.030
See you next time.

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:35.230
Thanks again.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:47.370
<b>Shinjuku Akakaze Circle</b>

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.580
Yuriko-san! Get ready to go on!

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.680
I leave tomorrow.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.430
Knowing that, will you still wait for me?

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:15.530
I will.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.900
I'll forever be here, waiting for your return.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.320
So please, come back...

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.520
I loved him with all my heart.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:30.400
So much that I want them to 
live the life they truly want.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.070
I will disappear quietly.

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:35.040
Even if a future

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.370
of darkness and solitude awaits.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.500
It will still be proof...

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.860
It will still be proof that I lived!

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.190
Looks like...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.940
Nogami Yuriko wasn't the murderer 
in the Schneider case.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.060
Nope.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:20.750
No actor could cry tears like 
those as a performance.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:26.130
What'd you find about Schneider's accomplices?

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:29.090
Just like you thought.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:33.720
I tailed the man removing the 
flowers from the theatre.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:38.560
He stopped at what looks 
like an ordinary florist's,

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.310
<b>Arekiyama Commerce Association</b>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.480
but the place doubles as a secret post

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.880
for Soviet spies to exchange intel.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:48.150
They communicate in code 
using a specific flower.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.050
In Russian, it's called

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:52.300
"romashka."

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:55.910
In Japan, it's commonly called "chamomile."

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.920
Two Soviet spies made contact with Schneider.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.880
One is the florist who collects the flowers.

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:05.340
And the other...

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.760
Nogami Yuriko's friend,

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.530
Yasuhara Miyoko.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.680
What tipped you off?

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.890
It was simple.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.360
The scent in Nogami's apartment
just after the murder

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.880
was the same as the flowers 
delivered to Yasuhara Miyoko.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.190
Meaning there was another connection

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:27.360
between Schneider and Yasuhara 
besides Nogami Yuriko.

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:30.620
Schneider probably planned to give

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:33.040
the movements of the Germans and Soviets

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.920
that he got from Japan to the British.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.300
And with the chance that 
he was now a triple agent,

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:41.850
the Soviets planned Schneider's assassination.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:46.130
They set things up to look like
suicide at his lover's apartment,

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:50.180
but to do so, Yasuhara Miyoko needed 
some time to be in there alone.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:52.600
After seeing Schneider's body,

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.110
Nogami rushed off in a panic 
to the police station

00:15:56.410 --> 00:16:00.390
while Miyoko put the prepared 
suicide note on the table.

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:04.060
The double cross in the English alphabet

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:08.570
might've been a message to 
the English-speaking side.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.370
How did she get the note, though?

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:17.000
Surely she didn't make him write it.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:20.700
Maybe she said it was a hint for 
the next code they would use?

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.320
The day it happened,

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:28.630
Miyoko knew Schneider would 
be in that apartment,

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.240
so she called him and said,

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.410
"At our next exchange,

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:36.100
I'll say, 'I've lost everything.

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:38.820
Let's die together,'

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.540
using the plant that carries that meaning."

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.370
Then,

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:47.290
while waiting for Yuriko to come home,

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:51.410
he figured he'd have a glass of wine.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:08.900
I'm told Yasuhara Miyoko confessed 
to Schneider's murder.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:13.710
The police send their thanks 
for the information.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:16.440
Quite a rare occurrence.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.560
Did Nogami Yuriko resemble...

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.490
Nishiyama Chizuru?

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:33.440
When Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki ordered 
me to monitor Karl Schneider,

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:36.600
and I first laid eyes on Nogami Yuriko,

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.370
I couldn't believe my eyes.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:43.540
Chizu-nee...

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.700
I never knew my parents' faces.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:51.380
I was left with my paternal grandparents,

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.890
but they were so advanced in age,

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:56.620
they couldn't be expected to care for a baby,

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:01.350
so it fell to the young daughter of 
a nearby farming family to raise me.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:03.820
Hiro-chan.

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.010
She, and she alone,

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:13.030
was the one person in the 
world who accepted me.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.780
Nishiyama Chizuru practically raised you.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:23.080
She eventually eloped with a 
young man who abandoned her,

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.760
and she never made it back to her 
hometown before dying of tuberculosis.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.330
When the target died,

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.960
you reported that you didn't notice.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.030
The only thing that could distract you,

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:37.250
a man trained by D-Agency,

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:40.360
would be the specter of Nishiyama Chizuru.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.300
It was a simple deduction.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:46.130
Because I was so focused on

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:48.350
Nogami Yuriko in that moment,

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:51.680
I failed to see the feelings of 
the other woman in the equation.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.580
You won't reconsider, correct?

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.740
Letter of resignation

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:07.330
Do you know why

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:10.920
D-Agency only takes men?

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.180
Because women kill even 
when it's not necessary.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.670
For foolish, trivial reasons

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:21.890
like love and hate.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:25.280
<i>Being completely unencumbered...</i>

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.360
<i>It requires</i>

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:30.350
<i>not believing in anything else in the world...</i>

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:34.920
<i>Abandoning trivial things like love and hate,</i>

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:38.030
<i>betraying what's in your 
heart that supports you,</i>

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:40.660
<i>and casting it aside.</i>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.820
<i>No matter how I tried,</i>

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:47.290
<i>I couldn't rid myself of Chizu-nee's memory.</i>

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:48.890
<i>No...</i>

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.260
<i>If I'd abandoned her,</i>

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.970
<i>I'd no longer be sure of my reason for living.</i>

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.070
<i>In the end,</i>

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.870
<i>I'll never be able to become
a monster like them.</i>

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.570
Shinjuku Akakaze Circle

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:28.290
<b>Reopening soon
with a new cast 
Don't miss it!</b>

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:29.620
Excuse me...

00:20:30.070 --> 00:20:32.830
Will Nogami Yuriko-san not be performing?

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.460
Oh, I remember you.

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:40.780
Yes, I'm afraid Yuriko-san quit.

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:41.730
She quit?

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:45.130
First she lost her boyfriend,

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:49.060
and then Miyoko-san got arrested...

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:52.430
It must've really taken a toll on her.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:54.720
I see...

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:59.720
It's so sad to think I'll never see 
Yuriko-san perform in Japan again.

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:02.800
Where is she going?

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:07.400
She said she wanted to start her 
acting studies over in a new place.

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:09.470
A movie studio wanted to sign her, too...

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:11.990
So she's going to Manchuria.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.070
Here's your dismissal.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.590
You've been to assigned to Kwantung.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:24.080
Apparently you'll be a lieutenant 
in a Manchurian unit.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:29.920
Lieutenant Tobisaki Hiroyuki.

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:34.580
Don't die.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:42.120
Are you stupid?

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:49.070
Who bows while wearing a business suit?
